--dir
.
--ignore=tmp/
--ignore=vendor/
--parser=prism
# rdoc's generated RBI reparents RDoc::Markup::Heading to Struct, conflicting with
# Sorbet's bundled payload definition. Unrelated to this project's own code.
--suppress-payload-superclass-redefinition-for=RDoc::Markup::Heading

# Lets a module declare the class it is mixed into (`requires_ancestor`), so a
# concern like Types::SecurityHoldings can call the methods graphql-ruby gives
# its host object and still be checked at `typed: strict`. This turns checking
# on rather than off: without it those calls are errors, and the alternative is
# an untyped escape hatch at each one.
--enable-experimental-requires-ancestor
